# DS3009: a glob that is not a valid pattern. The error points at the character.
mode: check
---- query
from '../../data/[a.csv' | take 1;
from '../../data/a**/x.csv' | take 1;
from '../../data/***.csv' | take 1
---- expected
error[DS3009]: `../../data/[a.csv` is not a valid glob pattern
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | from '../../data/[a.csv' | take 1;
  |                  ^ this `[` has no matching `]`
  |
  = note: in a glob, `*` and `?` match characters within a directory, `**` any number of directories, and `[abc]` one of the characters listed; to match `[` itself, write `[[]`

error[DS3009]: `../../data/a**/x.csv` is not a valid glob pattern
  --> query:2:19
  |
2 | from '../../data/a**/x.csv' | take 1;
  |                   ^ `**` must be a whole part of the path, as in `logs/**/x.csv`
  |
  = note: in a glob, `*` and `?` match characters within a directory, `**` any number of directories, and `[abc]` one of the characters listed; to match `[` itself, write `[[]`

error[DS3009]: `../../data/***.csv` is not a valid glob pattern
  --> query:3:20
  |
3 | from '../../data/***.csv' | take 1
  |                    ^ use `*` or `**`; three or more `*` in a row mean nothing
  |
  = note: in a glob, `*` and `?` match characters within a directory, `**` any number of directories, and `[abc]` one of the characters listed; to match `[` itself, write `[[]`
